// BML.lang: the language's own package, the one a BML unit imports as
// BML.lang.*. Object, String and the primitive types are the compiler's own
// (bml-hati-root-type? and bml-hati-primitive-types in grammars/bml.fk).
// Application is the base a program class with a main extends: the class
// model reads it as BML.lang.Application (bml-class-extends-structural?), and
// the thesis grammar (BMF-grammar.bml) and the compiler picture
// (bmf-bml-compiler-picture.bml) extend it.
//
// A program ends at its last statement, at a return, at a throw no catch
// holds, or at a fail no choose holds. A fail answers the choose around it;
// with no choice left, the program ends and answers the value of its last
// completed statement, the value it stood on, even when the fail lands in
// the middle of an expression. The thesis says a fail backtracks until
// another path is found (backtracking-model-languages.txt, 634) and leaves
// open what a program answers when no path is left; this is the reading that
// depends on no machine. The native lane voices such an ending once through
// the compiler organ (bml-run-heard in grammars/bml.fk).
package BML.lang;

class Application : Object { section [public] { } }
